  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">11th Manila International Dialogue on Human Trafficking</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Manila International Dialogue on Human Trafficking (MID) is a key platform established in 2015 that brings together over 30 foreign missions, multilateral organizations, Philippine government agencies, international partners, and civil society to combat human trafficking.

MID&apos;s goal is to advance discourse, inform programming, and drive policy reform to strengthen international cooperation. It achieves this through Technical Working Groups (including one on fishers/seafarers chaired by the Netherlands) and by hosting the Regional Meeting of Southeast Asian National Inter-Agency Committees on Trafficking. This regional meeting focuses on harmonizing policy and improving cooperation on regional cases among ASEAN states.

The 11th Plenary Session will focus on issues, trends, and good practices in international cooperation. Highlights will include the presentation of recommendations from the Technical Working Groups, TIPTalks featuring good practice in victim protection and justice.</narrative>
  </description>
